 "name": "einzel lens (r-z, three-tube) \u2014 Abdulla & Hussein 2020 geometry, decelerating mode",
 "notes": "Three-tube einzel lens, cylindrically symmetric, solved in r-z. Geometry after Abdulla & Hussein (2020): three coaxial tubes each 25 mm long, bores 30/24/30 mm diameter, with 6 mm axial overlap between adjacent tubes -- the tubes interleave rather than butting end-to-end, which keeps the gap fields short. Outer tubes grounded; the centre tube carries V2. This is the DECELERATING mode: a positive ion slows through the centre element and re-accelerates out, so the lens changes focal length WITHOUT changing the beam energy. Operating point: V2 = +57 V tuned for m/z 120 at 100 eV. Vacuum (no gas): this deck is about optics, not transport.",
